{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":124912,"duration_api_ms":124458,"num_turns":3,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"df817625-15b4-4fd2-a635-e10204d3aa58","total_cost_usd":0.51201425,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28119,"cache_read_input_tokens":84692,"output_tokens":2078,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28119,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2078,"cacheReadInputTokens":84692,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28119,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27005975000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":4182,"cacheReadInputTokens":122160,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38014,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2419545,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all 7 amendments against the codebase. Six identify real correctness, completeness, or consistency bugs. The performance amendment (fr-1-e6424ff8) is premature optimization — substrate_layers is 1-3 elements and the cost is negligible. Notably, the exploration revealed that TankSnapshot::from_state() already computes volume_l once locally but then calls TankState wrappers that recompute it internally, which slightly undermines the amendment's framing but doesn't change the conclusion: the overhead is trivial. The two most critical amendments are fr-1-f002ba49 (save schema compatibility) and fr-1-82e8bfe5 (gross-volume constructors), which represent incomplete edges of the gross-to-net volume refactor that will produce silent concentration errors.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-e8deb6c0","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: seeded_example() calls new() which seeds WaterState totals for the default substrate (3.0 cm single InertSand layer), then replaces substrate_layers with ActivePlanted(2.0) + CoarsePorous(1.0) = 3.0 cm total. The depths coincidentally match, but this is fragile — the two values are independently maintained with no structural coupling. If either changes, dissolved-mass totals become inconsistent with actual water volume. The fix (rescale or rebuild WaterState after setting layers) mirrors the existing pattern in apply_startup_overrides and is straightforward."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4cecd20d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: The unit test canonical_helpers_use_net_water_volume and the proptest helper_outputs_never_go_negative both test exactly 8 concentration helpers (TAN, nitrite, nitrate, DOC, DIC, DO, phosphate, alkalinity) plus substrate_volume_l and water_volume_l. Five concentration helpers — calcium_mg_per_l, magnesium_mg_per_l, gh_d, tds_mg_per_l, conductivity_us_cm — have zero test coverage. The acceptance criteria explicitly requires tests for every helper and non-negativity property tests for all. This is a clear, measurable gap that should be closed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-175e6bec","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total is a first-class field on WaterState, actively read/written in nitrogen_cycle.rs (DON production from detritus, Monod-kinetics consumption by decomposers, mineralization to TAN) and scaled in rescale_totals_for_volume. Every other actively-used dissolved species has a canonical concentration accessor. DON is the sole gap, and the downstream bead tanksim-6e5.2.3 (normalize nitrogen-cycle kinetics to concentration-based terms) directly requires it. Adding don_mg_n_per_l() follows the established pattern exactly."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-62a277eb","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: gh_d() exists as a proper helper on WaterState (line 146) and TankState (line 220), but kh_d() does not exist anywhere in the codebase. snapshot.rs line 73 computes KH inline as (state.alkalinity_meq_per_l() * 50.0) / 17.848. This is exactly the ad-hoc re-derivation pattern the helper system was designed to eliminate. The asymmetry (GH has a canonical helper, KH does not) is unjustified since both are standard aquarium chemistry measures. Adding kh_d() is low-risk and consistent."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-e6424ff8","decision":"reject","rationale":"The substrate_layers vector contains 1-3 elements in practice. Even with ~10 recomputations in from_state(), this is ~30 floating-point additions per snapshot — completely negligible. The snapshot is built once per simulation step, not in a tight loop. Introducing caching (with its invalidation complexity) or a ConcentrationView struct adds architectural weight for zero measurable benefit. This is textbook premature optimization. If substrate_layers ever grows to hundreds of elements, profiling data can justify the change then."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f002ba49","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: SCHEMA_VERSION remains 2, and from_json() does strict version equality matching with no migration path. The refactor switches all concentration reads to net water volume (TankState::water_volume_l subtracts substrate displacement), but existing schema-2 saves had their totals evolved under gross-volume semantics. Loading such a save unchanged and reading through net-volume helpers inflates all concentrations by the ratio gross/net. For a tank with 12L gross and 10L net, that's a 20% error on every chemistry parameter — a silent data corruption bug. Schema must be bumped with either rejection of old saves or migration of totals."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-82e8bfe5","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: default_for_geometry() and from_source_profile() both delegate to geometry.water_volume_l() which returns gross fill volume (no substrate deduction). WaterState::default() chains through default_for_geometry. Meanwhile TankState::new() correctly uses the net volume variant. Any external caller constructing WaterState directly via these geometry-based constructors for a substrate-bearing tank will seed dissolved-mass totals at gross volume, then have concentrations read at net volume — systematically inflating all mg/L values. These constructors must accept substrate depth or be marked internal to prevent bypassing the net-volume invariant."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7f32b908-12c2-4b8d-9e08-849f978ff667"}
